# Audit and project documentation location

## Audit documentation

All **audit documentation** must be written to `.cursor/docs/`:

- Security audits, secret audits, compliance notes
- Review summaries or audit reports generated by Cursor (Agent, CLI, or workflows)
- Any "audit" or "audit trail" style documentation for this project

**Do not** place audit docs in the repo root, in `docs/`, or in ad-hoc locations. Use **`.cursor/docs/`** only.

## Naming

- Use descriptive filenames, e.g. `secret-audit-2026-01-28.md`, `compliance-notes.md`, `review-summary-PR-123.md`.
- Prefer dated names when the doc is a point-in-time report.

## When creating or saving audit docs

When you generate or are asked to save audit-related documentation:

1. Create or update files under `.cursor/docs/`.
2. If the user asks for "audit documentation" without a path, default to `.cursor/docs/` and a sensible filename.
